  "id": "sensitive",
  "term": "sensitive",
  "definition": "In this social-psychological context, sensitive refers to an approach that takes account of people’s lived circumstances and structural inequalities when understanding selfhood, resilience, and agency. It emphasizes interpreting experience in relation to social position, adversity, and context rather than treating these as separate from the person.",
